","content":"none (territory of Australia)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:54","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"the flag of Australia is used; note - in early 1986, the Christmas Island Assembly held a design competition for an island flag, however, the winning design has never been formally adopted as the official flag of the territory","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:55","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Phosphate mining had been the only significant economic activity, but in December 1987 the Australian Government closed the mine. In 1991, the mine was reopened. With the support of the government, a $34 million casino opened in 1993. The casino closed in 1998. The Australian Government in 2001 agreed to support the creation of a commercial space-launching site on the island, projected to begin operations in the near future","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:56","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"NA","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:57","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"NA","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:58","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: NA\n\nindustry: NA\n\nservices: NA","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:59","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"NA","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:60","country":"CX","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force - by occupation","content":"NA","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/kt.html#field:61","country":"CX","edition_year":200